questions.explanation:
Box 1: {"fr", "de", "es"} — You only specify TARGET languages, not the source. The source language (en-GB) is set via SpeechRecognitionLanguage. English is NOT included as a target because the recognition already produces English text. You only need French, German, and Spanish as translation targets.

Box 2: TranslationRecognizer — After configuring SpeechTranslationConfig with source and target languages, you initialize a TranslationRecognizer (not SpeechRecognizer, which only does speech-to-text without translation).

Code pattern:
var config = SpeechTranslationConfig.FromSubscription(key, region);
config.SpeechRecognitionLanguage = "en-GB";
config.AddTargetLanguage("fr");
config.AddTargetLanguage("de");
config.AddTargetLanguage("es");
using var recognizer = new TranslationRecognizer(config);

Ref: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-services/speech-service/get-started-speech-translation
